&nbsp;","ISSA is looking for a Senior Manager, Lifecycle Marketing!

This is a 100% remote role, but you must reside in an ISSA-eligible state: AZ, CT, FL, GA, ID, IL, IN, MN, NC, NV, OH, OR, PA, SC, TN, TX, UT, VA, WI.

About ISSA: ISSA is an education and certification company for fitness trainers, personal trainers, strength and conditioning coaches, nutritionists, nutrition coaches, yoga instructors, health coaches, medical professionals, and more! For over 35 years, ISSA has developed a personal fitness training program that combines gym experience with practical and applied sciences. With over 300 employees, we have certified nearly 500,000 trainers in 174 countries. We were recently recognized as a Best Place to Work and Healthiest Employer by The Phoenix Business Journal, Fastest Growing Private Company by Inc. Southwest Regionals, and Top Workplace by USA Today!

We’re seeking a Senior Manager, Lifecycle Marketing to own and optimize the end-to-end customer journey across our portfolio of brands. This role blends strategic vision with hands-on execution, driving conversions, improving student retention, and maximizing lifetime value. You’ll lead lifecycle strategy from lead acquisition through onboarding, retention, and expansion, while managing a team of Email Marketing Specialists.

The ideal candidate has experience scaling lifecycle programs in a multi-brand environment, is equally comfortable developing a segmentation strategy as they are rolling up their sleeves to build campaigns, and thrives at the intersection of marketing, sales, and customer success.


So What's the Job?
Multi-brand lifecycle strategy: Define and execute segmented customer journeys across brands, product lines, and buyer personas (e.g., career switchers, upskillers).
Team leadership: Manage, mentor, and grow a team of Email Marketing Specialists, setting clear priorities, ensuring flawless execution, and fostering professional development.
Automation & personalization: Own the email/SMS/CRM automation roadmap (HubSpot or similar), building nurture, onboarding, retention, upsell, and reactivation campaigns that reduce friction and increase speed-to-purchase.
Cross-functional collaboration: Partner with Sales, Product, and Student Support to align lifecycle campaigns with revenue, retention, and customer success goals.
Testing & optimization: Design, launch, and analyze A/B tests on content, offers, and timing to improve funnel performance, while driving a test-and-learn culture.
Data-driven insights: Define KPIs, monitor lead stages, and analyze performance to uncover scalable growth levers, improve engagement, and maximize LTV.
Customer-first mindset: Champion the voice of the customer to ensure communications deliver value, build trust, and strengthen relationships.
Cross-brand coordination: Share best practices, frameworks, and efficiencies across multiple brand teams while maintaining tailored journeys for each audience.
Content & campaign execution: Partner with design and content teams to create on-brand ads, landing pages, email templates, SMS campaigns, and more.

What is ISSA looking for?
6–10 years in lifecycle, retention, CRM, or email marketing, preferably in education, DTC, or subscription businesses.
2+ years of people management experience with a track record of mentoring and developing talent.
Strong expertise with HubSpot, Marketo, or similar ESP/CRM platforms (certifications a plus).
Experience building segmentation frameworks, automated journeys, and personalized campaigns at scale.
Proficiency with A/B testing, reporting, and translating data into actionable insights.
Knowledge of email/SMS compliance regulations (e.g., CAN-SPAM, GDPR).
Excellent copywriting and/or creative skills, with an eye for engaging health and wellness audiences.
Strong communication and project management skills, comfortable working cross-functionally.
Passion for health, wellness, and helping others achieve their goals is a plus!
Anything else? Absolutely! Benefits and Perks:
This is a place where every day we are inspired by our teammates, encouraging each other to be our best. The environment is friendly and upbeat! And we feel it’s important to reward our team with competitive pay and benefits. Here are some of the highlights:

Free Certifications: Who wants to be their best self? WE DO! As an ISSA team member, you have access to our courses and certifications…at no expense! Additionally, you'll receive exclusive discounts on leading products in the fitness industry. Cool, right? After 90 days, employees can also enroll up to 5 friends/family members each year in our courses...FOR FREE!

Health & Wellness Reimbursement: If our company’s mission is to encourage healthy living, we need to walk the talk and ensure each employee is supported in their wellness journey! Employees can submit fitness purchases (gym membership, fitness equipment, classes) and professional and mental health purchases (personal learning courses, wellness apps, art classes, and more) for reimbursement up to $50/month…$600/year.

Work-Life Synergy: Our Core Team members have 3 weeks of PTO each year...accrued on a bi-weekly basis! And everyone at ISSA gets 8 paid national holidays every year...PLUS 1 floating holiday!

Parental Time Off: We support our team members as they grow their families! Once you qualify for FMLA, you are eligible to receive up to 6 weeks of paid maternity/paternity time to bond with a new child.

Well-Rounded Support: We are proud to offer Maven, a global platform that provides on-demand care! Maven provides an option for inclusive, comprehensive support for the whole employee and their family journey!

Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance: A key component to living a healthy lifestyle is having access to the care we (and our families) need. We offer 2 medical insurance plans accompanied by Health Saving Account (HSA) and Flexible Savings Account (FSA) options, as well as Dental and Vision coverage. And you don’t have to wait forever! Eligibility begins the 1st of the month after you start.

Team Building: We may be remote, but we don’t have to be alone! We host a monthly schedule of virtual team activities, town halls, brown bag lunches, and other special events…so many fun ways for us to connect and support one another.

Growth Opportunities: When our people grow…we grow! We offer leadership training, coaching/mentoring opportunities, and cross-functional collaboration on special projects and initiatives. Constant growth and development are inherent in our culture.

Tools To Do The Job: We ensure you are hooked up with the tools, equipment, and systems you need. We begin the process before your start date, so you are ready to rock ‘n roll on your first day. We also provide a monthly work-from-home allowance!

100% Remote Work: You can say goodbye to long commutes because all of our roles can be performed from the comfort of your own home. To connect and communicate more effectively, ISSA is a camera-friendly culture in which cameras are on for scheduled meetings. We have found that this bridges the gap that can exist since we are not working together in an office.

What Else? We have a 401(k) company match and 100% company-paid life/AD&D insurance/short-term disability. We also offer an employee assistance program to assist with work-life concerns (legal, financial, and mental health). Our ultimate goal is to support you and your overall wellness.

Transform your career at ISSA!"
