Executive Assistant to the Vice President
Assists the Vice President with implementation of activities and projects to support the College mission and strategic plan. Communicate directives verbally and in writing.
Facilitate meetings including scheduling, preparation of agendas, assembling and distributing support materials, and taking minutes.
Compile data and write reports as directed by the Vice President.
Assist in the preparation of Office of Academic Affairs communications including emails, letters, memoranda, and presentations.
Contact and receive calls from staff at all levels on behalf of the Vice President, answer questions, locate information for staff, interpreting district instructional policies, and evaluate issues in terms of priority. Facilitate problem-solving when the Vice President is absent.
Maintain a comprehensive Academic Affairs Outlook calendar.
Manage travel for the VP of Academic Affairs, function as the Concur delegate for review of all VP travel approvals for faculty and staff.
Develop, monitor, review, and reconcile office budgets and expenditures. Process external invoices. Enters requisitions and procurement card purchases for department.



Office of Academic Affairs Records Management.
Maintain the Office of Academic Affairs records retention plan, train division staff, and monitor compliance with the College Records Officer. Determine when files will be purged, and which will be designated for storage.
Track BTC submissions of WTCS Program action files and manage college records of WTCS actions. Produce the annual “Programs Approved for Operation” list for approval at the annual District Board meeting in January.
Responsible for maintaining confidential files.
