Remote",,"About ISACA: ISACA® (www.isaca.org) champions the global workforce advancing trust in technology. For more than 55 years, ISACA has empowered its community of 185,000+ members with the knowledge, credentials, training and network they need to thrive in fields like information security, governance, assurance, risk management, data privacy and emerging tech. With a presence in more than 190 countries and with nearly 230 chapters worldwide, ISACA offers resources tailored to every stage of members’ careers—helping them to thrive in a rapidly changing digital landscape, drive trusted innovation and ensure a more secure digital world. Through the ISACA Foundation, ISACA also expands IT and education career pathways, fostering opportunities to grow the next generation of technology professionals. Overview:
The Manager, Product Operations plays a critical leadership role in driving operational excellence across the product lifecycle—from development through delivery. This role is responsible for building and optimizing the frameworks, processes, and cross-functional collaboration necessary to scale and enhance product performance.

Acting as a strategic partner to Product Management, Publishing, Membership, IT, Sales, Marketing, and Sales Operations, this individual ensures alignment, clarity, and efficiency across all touchpoints that influence product success. The Manager will lead initiatives focused on process improvement, data-driven decision-making, and continuous optimization to accelerate time-to-market and elevate the overall product experience.
Responsibilities:
Leadership & Team Development
Provide strategic leadership, coaching, and mentorship to the product operations team, fostering a high-performance culture rooted in excellence, accountability, and continuous improvement. Champion effective communication, collaboration, and alignment both within the team and across key departments to drive cohesive execution of operational priorities.
Strategic Alignment & Lifecycle Optimization
Partner with senior product management to align operational practices with corporate objectives. Define and implement scalable, best-in-class processes for product setup, maintenance, and sunsetting. Lead initiatives that streamline lifecycle management and drive adoption of operational best practices across the organization.
Quality Assurance, Analytics & Process Improvement
Establish and oversee quality assurance standards to ensure products meet organizational expectations throughout their lifecycle. Define key performance indicators (KPIs) and collaborate with data analysts to deliver actionable dashboards and reporting. Monitor lifecycle stages and customer escalation channels (CEC) to identify trends, drive root cause analysis, and lead continuous improvement initiatives—including knowledge sharing and training—to reduce operational friction and support demands.
Cross-Functional Collaboration & Product Alignment
Act as the primary operational liaison across Product Management, Publishing, Membership, IT, Sales, Marketing, and Operations. Facilitate cross-functional coordination to support seamless product development, deployment, maintenance, and retirement, ensuring alignment with broader organizational goals and strategic priorities.
Drive Operational Excellence and Cross-Functional Execution
Evaluate and implement tools and technologies to enhance product operations efficiency, ensuring Fonteva and Salesforce product data remains accurate and up to date. Train teams on new processes to improve collaboration and productivity. Supervise cross-functional project management for product launches and updates, overseeing timelines, deliverables, and dependencies to support timely, successful releases. Maintain and communicate the product roadmap, prepare regular performance reports for senior management, manage operations budgets, and identify opportunities for cost optimization. Maintain comprehensive documentation of product operations processes to ensure consistency and transparency across the organization.
Other Job Functions
Drive continuous improvement initiatives to enhance product development and delivery efficiency.
Qualifications:
Required Field of Study:
Bachelor’s Degree in Business Administration, Operations Management, Product Management from an accredited university or equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience.
Minimum Years of Experience Required:
6–8 years of experience, including 2–3 years of people management or team leadership experience, with a proven track record of leading cross-functional teams and driving operational excellence
Description of Minimum Relevant Experience Required:
Background in data-driven decision-making, including the development of KPIs, dashboards, and reporting to measure operational effectiveness
Experience managing budgets and vendor relationships
Previous work experience as an operations manager, product operations manager
Familiarity with product management, operations management, pricing management, data analytics, and project management
Preferred Field of Study:
Master’s Degree in Business Administration, Operations Management, Product Management from an accredited university or equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience.
Preferred Years of Experience:
8+ Years of relevant professional experience with proven track record of successful team management and leadership
Description of Preferred Relevant Experience:
Experience managing operations at an association
Experience managing operations at a learning, content, or service product management organization
Experience working in an agile environment
Competencies/Skills Required:
Leadership & Collaboration
Strong people management skills with experience coaching, developing, and motivating high-performing teams
Proven ability to influence cross-functional teams without direct authority
Skilled at facilitating collaboration between departments such as Product, Marketing, IT, Sales, and Customer Success
Change management mindset, with the ability to lead teams through evolving priorities and systems
Strategic & Operational Thinking
Excellent strategic planning and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects and priorities simultaneously
Strong understanding of the product lifecycle and best practices in lifecycle management (development, launch, maintenance, sunset)
Experience building and optimizing scalable operational frameworks and process improvements
Analytical & Technical Skills
Proficient in data analysis and interpretation, with the ability to turn insights into actionable improvements
Familiarity with dashboarding and reporting tools; experience working with KPIs and performance metrics
Working knowledge of product management platforms (e.g., Jira, Aha!, Confluence) and CRM systems (e.g., Salesforce, Fonteva)
Comfortable with budgeting and cost analysis in operational environments
Communication & Documentation
Exceptional written and verbal communication skills
Skilled in developing clear, comprehensive process documentation and training materials
Ability to effectively present to senior leadership, providing insights, recommendations, and updates
Customer & Quality Focus
Strong customer-centric mindset, ensuring that operational processes support excellent product experiences
Commitment to quality assurance, risk mitigation, and continuous improvement
Occasional travel may be required for this role, particularly to attend company-sponsored events such as all-hands meetings and team offsites.
