&nbsp;","Job Description:
Your new career in healthcare technology sales begins here! Utilize your confidence, grit, and determination to connect with prospects and grow the organization’s new business pipeline. In this role, you will be the first point of contact with potential clients, conducting high-volume cold calls to engage healthcare professionals, introduce our solutions, and create opportunities for our sales team. Your goal is to spark interest, set up meetings, and contribute to the growth of our customer base.
What You'll Do:
Cold Calling & Outreach - Make a high volume of outbound calls and emails daily to engage healthcare decision-makers
Lead Qualification – Identify potential customers, identify problems we can solve, and qualify prospects based on fit and needs, and schedule meetings for the sales team
Product Education – Clearly communicate the value proposition of our healthcare tech solutions and address common objections
CRM Management – Maintain accurate records of all outreach efforts, conversations, and lead progress in Salesforce
Collaboration – Work closely with Account Executives and Marketing to refine messaging and optimize outreach strategies
Follow-ups & Nurturing – Conduct timely follow-ups with prospects and keep them engaged throughout the sales funnel
Market Research – Stay up to date on industry trends, competitor offerings, and customer pain points to tailor outreach efforts effectively
What You'll Bring:
Bachelor’s degree required. Must be located within Eastern or Central time zones.
Ability to demonstrate robust knowledge of and passion for sales
Confident, strong and energetic phone presence to engage prospects and peak interest
Persistence and resilience to handle objections and rejection, as well as meet goals
Highly self-motivated, goal-oriented, and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment
Nice to Have:
Previous experience in sales or business development
Cold outreach experience
Why Join Phreesia?
Tired of calculating your commission every month? If you’re motivated by the consistency of a competitive base salary, this role may be the perfect fit for you. You’ll have the opportunity to earn up to $60,000-$80,000 base salary during your tenure in the SDR role based on multiple factors such as previous experience, overall skills and competencies assessed during the interview process and internal equity.
Phreesia also offers:
Career growth opportunities in sales dev, sales, or other areas of the business
Comprehensive onboarding and ongoing education/training for continued success
Location: Remote (CST or EST) with easy access to a major airport offering direct domestic routes.
Who We Are:
At Phreesia, we’re looking for smart and passionate people to help drive our mission of creating a better, more engaging healthcare experience. We’re committed to helping healthcare organizations succeed in an ever-evolving landscape by transforming the way healthcare is delivered. Our SaaS platform digitizes appointment check-in and offers tools to engage patients, improve efficiency, optimize staffing, and enhance clinical care.
Phreesia cares about our employees by providing a diverse and dynamic work environment. We’re a five-time winner of Modern Healthcare Magazine’s Best Places to Work in Healthcare award and we’ve been recognized on the Bloomberg Gender Equality Index. We are dedicated to continuously improving our employee experience by launching new programs and initiatives. If you thrive in a culture of recognition, value inclusivity, professional development, and growth opportunities, Phreesia could be a great fit!
Top-rated Employee Benefits:
100% Remote work + home office expense reimbursements
Competitive compensation
Flexible PTO + 8 company holidays
Monthly reimbursement for cell phone + internet + wellness
100% Paid 12-week parental leave to our U.S. employees, as well as a generous parental benefit to our employees in Canada
Variety of insurance coverage for people (and pets!)
Continuing education and professional certification reimbursement
Opportunity to join an Employee Resource Group.
We strive to provide a diverse and inclusive environment and are an equal opportunity employer."
