Job Description:

Job Title: Executive Administrative Assistant

Location: Remote
Employment Type: Full-time

About the Role

We are seeking a sharp, proactive, and highly organized Executive Administrative Assistant (EA) to provide seamless support at the leadership level. This is a high-impact role requiring exceptional communication, executive presence, discretion, and sound judgment. You will serve as a trusted partner, gatekeeper, and problem-solver—helping leaders operate at maximum effectiveness and focus on strategic priorities.

Key Responsibilities

Executive Support

Manage complex calendars across multiple time zones, coordinating meetings and engagements with internal and external stakeholders.
Prioritize and organize a heavy flow of requests, travel, and events.
Prepare and edit correspondence, communications, presentations, and related materials.
Handle sensitive information with the utmost integrity and discretion.

Operational Efficiency

Track and follow up on key action items, decisions, and deadlines from meetings.
Organize and support leadership meetings, ensuring flawless logistics, briefing materials, and document preparation.
Create executive summaries, agendas, and pre-meeting documentation.
Anticipate needs and proactively remove roadblocks to enhance operational effectiveness.

Communication & Liaison

Serve as a primary point of contact between leaders and internal/external stakeholders.
Draft and review high-quality communications on behalf of executives.
Manage inboxes and assist in prioritization and correspondence.
Communicate with clarity and professionalism across all levels of the organization.

Travel Coordination

Coordinate and manage domestic and international travel logistics, including itineraries, accommodations, and visa requirements.

Project Coordination

Support special projects, research, and strategic initiatives with tight deadlines and high visibility.
Collaborate cross-functionally with teams to ensure execution and alignment on organizational priorities

Qualifications

Required

7+ years of experience supporting C-level or senior executives in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment.
Experience in a professional services, consulting, or large corporate environment with client-facing exposure.
Outstanding organizational, time management, and multitasking skills.
Ability to quickly learn and apply new technologies, including AI-driven tools.
Strong interpersonal skills and high emotional intelligence.
Excellent written and verbal communication skills.
Comfortable working in dynamic and ambiguous environments with a proactive, solution-oriented mindset.
Proficient in Microsoft PowerPoint, Word, Excel, and modern productivity tools.

Preferred

Experience preparing leadership or board-level briefing materials and interacting with senior stakeholders.
Global exposure with experience managing across multiple time zones and cultures.
Familiarity with governance, executive communications, or strategic planning processes.
Bachelor’s degree or equivalent professional experience.
Proficiency with enterprise tools such as Microsoft O365, Concur, Salesforce, or similar systems.

